    <%/* ─── FAQ ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */%>
    <div purpose="faq-section">
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div purpose="faq" class="d-flex flex-column">
        <div purpose="accordion" class="d-flex flex-column justify-content-start">
            <div purpose="accordion-body">
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="patch-faq__header1" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#patch-faq__body1" aria-controls="patch-faq__body1">
                  What are Fleet-maintained apps?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="patch-faq__body1" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="patch-faq__header1">
                  Fleet maintains installation metadata for a growing catalog of apps, like Chrome, Firefox, Slack, Zoom, and Office, across macOS and Windows. Add them to Fleet and install them on your hosts without any additional configuration. To learn more, check out the <a href="/guides/fleet-maintained-apps">Fleet-maintained apps guide</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="patch-faq__header2" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#patch-faq__body2" aria-controls="patch-faq__body2">
                  How does Fleet keep Fleet-maintained apps safe?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="patch-faq__body2" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="patch-faq__header2">
                  Installers come straight from the vendor and are verified against a pinned SHA-256 hash. Every catalog change is installed and uninstalled on real hosts and reviewed by a person before release, and any version that fails testing is held back.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="patch-faq__header3" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#patch-faq__body3" aria-controls="patch-faq__body3">
                  How do patch policies work?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="patch-faq__body3" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="patch-faq__header3">
                  A patch policy checks whether each Fleet-maintained app is up to date on your hosts. Fleet runs policy checks on a typical one-hour cadence across all online hosts. The first time a host fails a patch policy, Fleet automatically sends an install request. To learn more, check out the guide to <a href="/guides/automatic-software-install-in-fleet">automatic software install</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="patch-faq__header4" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#patch-faq__body4" aria-controls="patch-faq__body4">
                  What if an app isn’t in the Fleet catalog?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="patch-faq__body4" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="patch-faq__header4">
                  Upload your own custom packages, and configure custom installation scripts if you need them. The same policy automation applies either way. To learn more, check out the guide to <a href="/guides/deploy-software-packages">deploying software packages</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="patch-faq__header5" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#patch-faq__body5" aria-controls="patch-faq__body5">
                  Which operating systems does Fleet patch?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="patch-faq__body5" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="patch-faq__header5">
                  Fleet manages software on <a href="/apple">macOS</a>, <a href="/windows">Windows</a>, and <a href="/linux">Linux</a> from a single place, with the same patch policies and the same automation.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="patch-faq__header6" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#patch-faq__body6" aria-controls="patch-faq__body6">
                  Can I use AI to patch devices?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="patch-faq__body6" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="patch-faq__header6">
                  Yes. Fleet works natively with your team’s AI tools, like Claude, Copilot, or any AI harness. Ask which devices are running a vulnerable version, and AI proposes the fix. A person on your team approves every change before it touches a device.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="d-flex flex-row justify-content-start">
              <p purpose="contact-note">Have another question? <a href="/docs/get-started/faq">Read the full FAQ</a> or <a href="/contact">talk to an engineer</a>.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
